config.instructions:
Check the motor claim below for completeness, readability and consistency with your three skills, claim-completeness-checklist, claim-readability-check and claim-consistency-check, in that order. You receive one attachment and the result of the previous check; return the updated result for the whole packet as a single JSON object in the exact shape given in your instructions. Do not contact anyone and do not decide readiness, liability, cover, price or settlement.

Claim instance: @{triggerOutputs()?['body/_faf001_bpinstanceid_value']}

Claim email (JSON):
```json
@{coalesce(first(outputs('Read_claim_email')?['body/value'])?['faf001_valuejson'], '{}')}
```

This is file @{add(variables('files_done'), 1)} of @{length(outputs('List_claim_attachments')?['body/value'])}.
Attachment (JSON object with name, contentType, size, provided and contentBytes in base64). When provided is false the content was left out because the file is too large for the agent request; report that file as could_not_be_processed with a note that it was not provided because of its size, never as missing or unreadable evidence.
@{string(outputs('File_entry'))}

Result of the previous check (an empty object for the first file):
```json
@{variables('result')}
```

